The '''Sanity Skip''' was a [[hyperspace route]] located in the [[Outer Rim Territories]]<ref name="Smuggler's Guide" /> and [[the Slice]].<ref name="Slice" /> One terminus was the [[Kessel system]]<ref name="Smuggler's Guide" /> in the [[Kessel sector]]<ref name="CGttSWG" /> within grid square T-10 of the [[Standard Galactic Grid]].<ref name="Appendix">{{GalaxyMapAppendix}}</ref> The other was the [[Oseon system]] in the [[Centrality]],<ref name="Smuggler's Guide" /> a sector in grid square T-8.<ref name="Appendix" /> The Kessel system acted as a junction from the Sanity Skip on to both [[the Channel]], a part of the larger [[Kessel Run]],<ref name="Tales from Vandor" /> and the [[Pabol Sleheyron]] trade routes.<ref name="Where" /> Another [[hyperspace route]] connected the Oseon system to the [[Junkfort Station system]].<ref name="TFABG">[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens Beginner Game|''Star Wars: The Force Awakens'' Beginner Game]] </ref><ref name="Junkfort">Per {{EmailCite|email=File:AtlasEmail-2025-09-03.png|creator=[[Jason Fry]]|date=2025-09-03}}, [[Junkfort Station]]'s absence on the [[Star Wars Galaxy Map|''Star Wars'' Galaxy Map]] is due to spacing limitations with the neighboring [[Marleyvane]] label, and Junkfort Station is located at the junction of the two [[hyperspace route]]s.</ref>

By [[10 BBY]],<ref name="Date">The entry in ''[[Star Wars: Smuggler's Guide]]'' mentioning the Sanity Skip is placed chronologically prior to an entry written by the criminal [[Tobias Beckett]]. ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates Beckett's [[death]] to [[10 BBY]], and so his entry in the guide and those chronologically before it must all be set by 10 [['ABY-BBY' dating system|BBY]].</ref> the [[Pirate Queen|pirate queen]] [[Maz Kanata]] marked the Sanity Skip as one of the "real" trade routes to be used by [[smuggler]]s, as opposed to the official routes, on a [[map]] that she included in the [[book]] known as the ''[[Smuggler's Guide]]''.<ref name="Smuggler's Guide" /> 

==Behind the scenes==
The Sanity Skip was first mentioned in ''[[Star Wars: Smuggler's Guide]]'', a reference book written by [[Daniel Wallace]] and released in [[2018]].<ref name="Smuggler's Guide" />

